  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Danidas engagement and campaign activities, since 2022. F2: 2022-16840</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Danish public support for development cooperation is increasing &#x2014; for the first time for many years. Support and awareness of the SDGs have increased, especially among younger audiences. It is positive and we need to build on it. But it is also clear that Danes&#x2019; knowledge of the development of the world&#x2019;s poorest countries remains limited and now we also see a tendency of polarisation. In between the two poles is a group of around 30% of Danes who are open for influence. This group needs to be targeted in order to maintain or increase public support for development cooperation, but also to make more people actively engaged in a more sustainable world. Campaign activities are one of the tools used by the MFA Engagement Team to reach out to this new target groups.</narrative>
  </description>
